      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Myophosphorylase deficiency (McArdle disease) is characterized by exercise intolerance that usually starts in childhood. Severe cramps and myoglobinuria are rarely problems in children. We describe an 8-year-old boy with exercise-induced myoglobinuria; he was homozygous for the mutation most commonly encountered in patients with typical McArdle disease."},
